I get off the bus.
This is the center of the city.
There is heavy traffic here.
There are many roads here.
I do not understand the way.
I see a traffic police officer.
I walk towards him.
"Hello, sir," I say.
"Which is the way to the Marine Drive walkway?" I ask.
He points to a wide road.
"Go straight down this road," he says.
"Then turn left," he says.
"The walkway is there," he says.
"Thank you, sir," I say.
I walk towards that wide road.
I walk straight.
I look for the left turn.
